  - ito-compute, Ito Compute, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill ito-compute, .agents/skills/ito-compute, assess_for_task, "Query live GPU inventory, submit an authenticated Itô fixed-rate RFQ, inspect RFQ or procurement status, revoke device credentials, and run explicitly gated node qualification through the separately installed canonical CLI. Use when a user asks to find H100/H200 capacity, request a fixed compute rate, check Itô compute status, validate GPU nodes, revoke Itô access, or rent or purchase GPU compute and needs the supported boundary explained."
  - ito-inference, Ito Inference, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill ito-inference, .agents/skills/ito-inference, assess_for_task, "Inspect the availability of model serving on a completed Itô compute booking and, when the canonical backend becomes available, hand off an explicitly confirmed serving manifest. Use after ito-compute has booked GPU nodes and the user asks for an OpenAI-compatible endpoint, ito-serve, hosted Kimi, or self-hosted open-weights inference. ECC implements no serving stack of its own."
  - ito-training, Ito Training, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill ito-training, .agents/skills/ito-training, assess_for_task, "Inspect the availability of ML training on a completed Itô compute booking and, when the canonical backend becomes available, hand off an explicitly confirmed training manifest. Use after ito-compute has booked GPU nodes and the user wants pre-training, fine-tuning, or RL on that metal. ECC implements no training stack of its own."
  - jake-arena-arena, Jake Arena Arena, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-arena-arena, .agents/skills/jake-arena-arena, assess_for_task, "Make 100 versions of Claude fight to the death over one task. Spins up N sub-agents (default 100, --quick for 16), gives every one the exact same task plus a different strategy card (reasoning mode, workflow, strategy), then runs a single-elimination bracket: they attack each other's solutions, defend and revise, and a judge scores every match on a written rubric until one solution survives. Use when the user is not satisfied with an answer, calls it a bad answer, says try again or do better, says ""arena"", or asks to make them compete."
  - jake-chatgpt-youtube-yt-audit, Jake Chatgpt Youtube Yt Audit, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-chatgpt-youtube-yt-audit, .agents/skills/jake-chatgpt-youtube-yt-audit, assess_for_task, "Audit a YouTube channel end to end - packaging, consistency, the first fifteen seconds, and what to fix first. Use for ""audit my channel"", ""why isn't my channel growing"", ""review my videos"", or a pasted channel URL."
  - jake-chatgpt-youtube-yt-chapters, Jake Chatgpt Youtube Yt Chapters, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-chatgpt-youtube-yt-chapters, .agents/skills/jake-chatgpt-youtube-yt-chapters, assess_for_task, "Write YouTube chapters from a transcript, validated against YouTube's own rules so they actually render. Use for ""add chapters"", ""timestamps"", ""break this video into sections""."
  - jake-chatgpt-youtube-yt-comment, Jake Chatgpt Youtube Yt Comment, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-chatgpt-youtube-yt-comment, .agents/skills/jake-chatgpt-youtube-yt-comment, assess_for_task, "Draft replies to YouTube comments in the creator's voice, triaged by which ones are worth answering. Use for ""reply to my comments"", ""handle the comment section"", ""someone asked X"", or a pasted comment thread."
  - jake-chatgpt-youtube-yt-edit, Jake Chatgpt Youtube Yt Edit, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-chatgpt-youtube-yt-edit, .agents/skills/jake-chatgpt-youtube-yt-edit, assess_for_task, "Turn a raw recording's transcript into an edit decision list - dead air, filler cues and retakes, with timecodes. Use for ""edit this"", ""cut the dead space"", ""tighten this video"", ""I rambled"", or any request to shorten footage from a transcript."
  - jake-chatgpt-youtube-yt-package, Jake Chatgpt Youtube Yt Package, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-chatgpt-youtube-yt-package, .agents/skills/jake-chatgpt-youtube-yt-package, assess_for_task, "Write and lint the title and thumbnail for a YouTube video as one pairing, checking truncation, duplication and vagueness before publish. Use for ""title ideas"", ""what should I call this"", ""thumbnail text"", ""my CTR is bad"", packaging, or any request to rename or repackage an existing video."
  - jake-chatgpt-youtube-yt-plan, Jake Chatgpt Youtube Yt Plan, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-chatgpt-youtube-yt-plan, .agents/skills/jake-chatgpt-youtube-yt-plan, assess_for_task, "Plan a week or a month of YouTube uploads - what to post, when, and in what order, sized to the creator's actual capacity. Use for ""plan my week"", ""content calendar"", ""what should I post"", ""I have no idea what to make next""."
  - jake-chatgpt-youtube-yt-retention, Jake Chatgpt Youtube Yt Retention, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-chatgpt-youtube-yt-retention, .agents/skills/jake-chatgpt-youtube-yt-retention, assess_for_task, "Read a YouTube Studio audience-retention export and find where viewers actually leave, then say what to change. Use for ""why do people stop watching"", ""my retention is bad"", a pasted retention chart or CSV, or ""fix my pacing""."
  - jake-chatgpt-youtube-yt-script, Jake Chatgpt Youtube Yt Script, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-chatgpt-youtube-yt-script, .agents/skills/jake-chatgpt-youtube-yt-script, assess_for_task, "Write a YouTube video script from a raw idea - hook options off 21 formulas, scored, then the full spoken script with the retention beats marked. Use whenever the user wants a video script, a hook, an opening line, ""what should I say"", ""write my next video"", or is about to record and does not have the first fifteen seconds yet."
  - jake-chatgpt-youtube-yt-seo, Jake Chatgpt Youtube Yt Seo, Technical SEO, SEO & Discovery, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-chatgpt-youtube-yt-seo, .agents/skills/jake-chatgpt-youtube-yt-seo, assess_for_task, "Write the description, tags and search-facing text for a YouTube video, aimed at the query a real person types. Use for ""write my description"", ""tags"", ""SEO"", ""help this video get found"", ""nobody is finding this""."
  - jake-chatgpt-youtube-yt-shorts, Jake Chatgpt Youtube Yt Shorts, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-chatgpt-youtube-yt-shorts, .agents/skills/jake-chatgpt-youtube-yt-shorts, assess_for_task, "Find the Shorts hiding inside a long video and write them, using the transcript to pick self-contained moments. Use for ""cut this into shorts"", ""clip this"", ""repurpose this video"", ""what should I clip""."
  - jake-chatgpt-youtube-yt-viral, Jake Chatgpt Youtube Yt Viral, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-chatgpt-youtube-yt-viral, .agents/skills/jake-chatgpt-youtube-yt-viral, assess_for_task, "Find what is actually working in the user's niche on YouTube and rank it by how far each video beat its own channel, then name the formula. Use for ""what's working right now"", ""find viral videos in my niche"", ""why did this blow up"", competitor research, or a swipe file."
  - jake-closer-contract-writer, Jake Closer Contract Writer, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-closer-contract-writer, .agents/skills/jake-closer-contract-writer, assess_for_task, "Contract Writer. Creates the contract and sends it over for you, after your yes. Turns what was agreed on the call into a plain-English services agreement (services, fee, term, launch, payment, ownership, liability, signature lines), checks the fee against what was actually said on the call or in the proposal, writes a print-ready PDF, drafts the email to send it, and marks the deal won when the signed copy comes back. Use when the user says ""write the contract"", ""send the agreement"", ""draft a services agreement"", ""send the paperwork"", ""they said yes"", or ""they signed""."
  - jake-closer-follow-up, Jake Closer Follow Up, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-closer-follow-up, .agents/skills/jake-closer-follow-up, assess_for_task, "Follow-Up. Keeps following up until a call is booked, then stops. Every morning it reads closer/pipeline.json and says who is due a follow-up today, who replied and is waiting on you, who booked, and who is stopped and why. Drafts each follow-up (a bump, then something useful, then a polite last note), waits for your yes, logs it, and stops at the first ""no"", the moment a call is booked, after 3 follow-ups or 30 days. Use when the user says ""follow up"", ""who do I need to follow up with"", ""they haven't replied"", ""chase"", ""nudge"", ""bump this"", ""they replied"", or every morning."
  - jake-closer-forecaster, Jake Closer Forecaster, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-closer-forecaster, .agents/skills/jake-closer-forecaster, assess_for_task, "Forecaster. Tells you what you'll close this month. Reads every open deal on the board with its stage, value and close date and gives three numbers: commit (contracts out), likely (each deal weighted by the chance for its stage) and best case, deal by deal, plus what you have already won. Shows your real win rate and how long deals take once you have history, and flags what makes the forecast wrong: past close dates, deals with no close date, deals gone quiet. Use when the user says ""forecast"", ""what will I close this month"", ""how's the month looking"", ""revenue projection"", ""win rate"", ""pipeline value"", or at the start of each week."
  - jake-closer-pipeline, Jake Closer Pipeline, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-closer-pipeline, .agents/skills/jake-closer-pipeline, assess_for_task, "Pipeline Manager. Keeps every deal moving on one board, the CRM the other ten Closer skills share: contacts, deals, stages (lead, contacted, replied, call-booked, proposal, contract-sent, won, lost), every email and call, next steps and a do-not-contact list, all in one plain closer/pipeline.json in your project. Shows the board, one deal's history, moves deals between stages, and validates the file after every change. Use when the user says ""pipeline"", ""board"", ""my deals"", ""CRM"", ""where are we with X"", ""move X to proposal"", ""we won X"", ""we lost X"", ""set up the closer skill"", or wants to replace Salesforce or HubSpot."
  - jake-closer-proposal-writer, Jake Closer Proposal Writer, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-closer-proposal-writer, .agents/skills/jake-closer-proposal-writer, assess_for_task, "Proposal Writer. Turns the call into a priced proposal the same day. Uses the prospect's own words from the call notes and replies, lays out what you will do, gives two or three clearly priced options (a full build, a monthly plan) with first-year totals, says what it pays back in one true line, recommends one, and ends with a single next step. Drafts the email; it goes out on your yes. Use when the user says ""write a proposal"", ""send pricing"", ""put together a quote"", ""they asked for prices"", ""send options"", or after a good call."
  - jake-closer-prospector, Jake Closer Prospector, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-closer-prospector, .agents/skills/jake-closer-prospector, assess_for_task, "Prospector. Finds new leads and performs the cold outreach. Builds a list of local businesses from public listings, checks each one's own website for the gap you fix (no online booking, not mobile-friendly, slow, no Google Ads tag, no reviews, no online ordering), ranks them with the reason, puts the best on the board, and writes a short, specific, honest opening email for each one with the legal footer and an opt-out. Every email waits for your yes. Use when the user says ""find me leads"", ""find customers"", ""prospect"", ""cold email"", ""cold outreach"", ""build a lead list"", ""who should I reach out to"", or ""get me new clients""."
  - jake-closer-record-keeper, Jake Closer Record Keeper, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-closer-record-keeper, .agents/skills/jake-closer-record-keeper, assess_for_task, "Record Keeper. Logs every email and call for you, so you never update a CRM by hand again. Reads your inbox through the Gmail connector, matches every message to a contact on the board, and logs it (opening, follow-up or reply) into closer/pipeline.json; logs calls with their notes saved to closer/calls/; shows the full timeline with anyone; and lists new addresses writing in that are not contacts yet. Use when the user says ""log this"", ""log my emails"", ""sync my inbox"", ""update the CRM"", ""what's my history with X"", ""save the call notes"", or at the end of every call and every morning."
  - jake-closer-researcher, Jake Closer Researcher, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-closer-researcher, .agents/skills/jake-closer-researcher, assess_for_task, "Researcher. Reads up on every prospect before the call. Reads the business's own public website (home, about, services, team, contact), pulls out the facts (how they describe themselves, what they offer, how long they have been open, their rating, phone, socials, which booking or ordering tools they use and which they do not) and writes a one-page brief to closer/research/ with talking points and questions to ask, every fact with its source. Use when the user says ""research X"", ""prep me for my call"", ""what do we know about X"", ""look into this lead"", ""brief me"", or before any booked call."
  - jake-closer-sales-coach, Jake Closer Sales Coach, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-closer-sales-coach, .agents/skills/jake-closer-sales-coach, assess_for_task, "Sales Coach. Listens to your sales call and tells you exactly what to say next. Reads the call's live captions (Google Meet's own captions, read off the page by Claude in Chrome, or any captions file), and the moment the other side raises an objection (""it's too expensive"", ""let me think about it"", ""I need to ask my partner"", ""we already have someone"") it shows you, and only you, the answer to say next, filled from your real offer. Also flags buying signals and questions you still owe an answer, and reviews the call afterwards (talk time, questions asked, next step). Use when the user says ""coach me on this call"", ""listen to my call"", ""I have a sales call"", ""what do I say if they say it's too expensive"", ""objection"", ""handle objections"", or ""review my call""."
  - jake-closer-scheduler, Jake Closer Scheduler, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-closer-scheduler, .agents/skills/jake-closer-scheduler, assess_for_task, "Scheduler. Puts every booked call on your calendar. Reads a reply like ""Thursday at 2 works"" and turns it into the right date and time, checks your calendar for a clash, offers open slots when they ask ""when are you free?"", creates the invite with a Google Meet link from your own calendar after your yes, confirms by email, and moves the deal to call-booked so follow-ups stop. Use when the user says ""book it"", ""schedule a call"", ""put it on my calendar"", ""send an invite"", ""when am I free"", ""they said Thursday works"", or when /follow-up shows a reply with a time."
  - jake-closer-win-back, Jake Closer Win Back, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-closer-win-back, .agents/skills/jake-closer-win-back, assess_for_task, "Win-Back. Brings back the deals that went quiet. Finds lost deals worth one more try (bad timing, budget, still thinking, no decision) once enough time has passed or on the date they asked you to come back, plus open deals that went silent after every follow-up, and writes one short, honest check-in from the reason it was lost. One win-back per deal, never to anyone who said no or unsubscribed. Use when the user says ""win back"", ""revive old deals"", ""follow up on lost deals"", ""who went quiet"", ""re-engage"", ""dead leads"", or once a week."
  - jake-console-console-anywhere, Jake Console Console Anywhere, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-console-console-anywhere, .agents/skills/jake-console-console-anywhere, assess_for_task, "Play Anywhere. Builds the port for Windows, Mac, Linux, Steam Deck, Android and PS Vita and packages it without any game files inside. doctor checks this machine's tools for a target and prints the exact install command for anything missing; plan prints the build steps taken from PS2Recomp's own README, android/README.md and vita scripts; package makes a player folder in console/dist/ (the runner, its libraries, an empty game/ folder, PLAYERS.md, a launch script, .recomp.json) and refuses outright if a disc image, PS2 ELF, IRX module, recompiled runner source or other game data is inside; guard runs that check on any folder; recomp-json writes the project's optional .recomp.json. Use when the user says ""put it on my Steam Deck"", ""build it for Android"", ""play it on my phone"", ""on my TV"", ""Vita build"", ""Mac build"", ""package it"", ""make a release folder"", ""is it safe to zip this"", or after the port plays on the machine it was built on."
  - jake-console-console-backend, Jake Console Console Backend, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-console-console-backend, .agents/skills/jake-console-console-backend, assess_for_task, "Backend Engineer. Builds the engine room the recompiled game runs on: syscalls, kernel stubs, file and disc I/O, the IOP. Reads PS2Recomp runtime logs and turns every ""Unimplemented PS2 stub"", ""[Syscall TODO]"", missing function, unhandled IOP RPC, failed disc read and untranslated instruction into a ranked fix list: count, first PC and RA, and the exact fix tool (a TOML binding, the runtime .cpp file to implement it in, an entry point and a recompile, or a game override). With the user's PS2Recomp checkout it reads the real handler names and syscall numbers. Writes nothing into the checkout; prints a table for console/STATE.md. Use when the user says ""unimplemented stub"", ""syscall TODO"", ""it crashes at boot"", ""fix the backend"", ""it can't find a file"", ""the IOP"", ""what is syscall 0x3C"", or after /console-tester reports a stop."
  - jake-console-console-controller, Jake Console Console Controller, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-console-console-controller, .agents/skills/jake-console-console-controller, assess_for_task, "Controller Mapper. Hooks the game up to any controller: DualSense, Xbox, Switch Pro, keyboard or touch, remapped how you like. Reads a mapping in console/controls.json (a layout preset plus per-button overrides, radial deadzone, invert Y, stick swap, analog trigger threshold, keyboard keys, two players, Android touch zones) and writes console/ps2_pad.cpp, a drop-in replacement for PS2Recomp's ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_pad.cpp with the same class, signature and DualShock 2 report. Optional input replay and recording for scripted test runs. Backs up the stock file before installing and only touches the PS2Recomp checkout you name. Use when the user says ""my controller doesn't work"", ""remap the buttons"", ""use my Xbox pad"", ""Switch Pro buttons are swapped"", ""invert the camera"", ""keyboard controls"", ""two players"", ""touch controls on Android"", or when /console-tester needs scripted input."
  - jake-console-console-graphics, Jake Console Console Graphics, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-console-console-graphics, .agents/skills/jake-console-console-graphics, assess_for_task, "Graphics Artist. Rebuilds the graphics: dumps every texture, lets you repaint or replace them with your own art, finds the widescreen fix. Converts PS2 TIM2 textures (.tm2, 32/24/16-bit and 8/4-bit indexed) from the user's own extracted disc to PNG, rebuilds them from edited PNGs at the same size and format (GS registers kept, palettes refit or quantised), finds TIM2 blobs inside archives and puts edited ones back, and lists the 4:3 aspect and FOV constants in the ELF with 16:9 pnach lines to try in PCSX2. Reads the packets the game sends the GS from a RAM dump (DMA chains, VIF codes, GIF tags, every register write) and flags what breaks rendering. Writes to console/textures/ and console/patches/, never into the disc image. Use when the user says ""dump the textures"", ""repaint"", ""replace this texture"", ""my own art"", ""HD textures"", ""make it widescreen"", ""16:9"", ""the picture is stretched"", ""black screen"", ""garbage textures"", ""nothing draws"", or ""how does the port draw""."
  - jake-console-console-levels, Jake Console Console Levels, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-console-console-levels, .agents/skills/jake-console-console-levels, assess_for_task, "Level Designer. Maps the disc's data files, unpacks the archives the levels live in, and swaps in your edits. Inventories an extracted PS2 disc (size, type by magic, entropy, a table-of-contents guess with a confidence score), unpacks CRI AFS archives and detected table-of-contents archives into a folder with an index.json, repacks them in the same order and alignment (keeping every offset when your edits fit), diffs two files or folders to show which bytes a change touched, lists strings, and reads the port's log to show which disc files a level loads. Writes under console/ and never modifies the original disc files. Use when the user says ""where are the levels"", ""unpack this archive"", ""what's in DATA.BIN"", ""edit the level"", ""swap in my map"", ""what changed between these two files"", ""which files does stage 3 load"", or before /console-graphics or /console-sound needs a file that sits inside an archive."
  - jake-console-console-mod, Jake Console Console Mod, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-console-console-mod, .agents/skills/jake-console-console-mod, assess_for_task, "Mod Maker. Describe any change in plain English and Claude builds it into the game: patches, cheats, new behaviour, as code that never touches the original files. Ports PCSX2 .pnach patches to the PS2Recomp port (code writes become ps2_recomp TOML instruction patches, data writes become a C++ game override that writes RDRAM at load or every frame, the rest are flagged for a manual port with the reason) and scaffolds game overrides that bind, replace or wrap a game function with the real PS2Recomp API. Writes to console/patches/, never to the game's files, the generated runner/*.cpp or headers. Use when the user says ""mod this game"", ""add a cheat"", ""infinite health"", ""port this pnach"", ""make my gun do X"", ""change how X works"", ""game override"", ""turn this PCSX2 patch into the port"", or once the port boots and they want to change it."
  - jake-console-console-physics, Jake Console Console Physics, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-console-console-physics, .agents/skills/jake-console-console-physics, assess_for_task, "Physics Tuner. Finds the numbers that decide how the game moves (speed, gravity, grip, jump height, frame rate) and tunes them. Scans the user's own game ELF for a float32 value stored in data or built in code (lui, ori or addiu, then mtc1), shows the instructions that read it, lists frame-timing candidates, and prints the exact pnach lines to test a new value in PCSX2 plus the PS2Recomp fix (TOML instruction patches or the data write /console-mod bakes in). Reads only; writes nothing. Use when the user says ""make the car faster"", ""lower the gravity"", ""jump higher"", ""more grip"", ""change the damage"", ""wider camera"", ""unlock 60 fps"", ""find the speed value"", or when /console-mod needs a number found."
  - jake-console-console-reverse, Jake Console Console Reverse, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-console-console-reverse, .agents/skills/jake-console-console-reverse, assess_for_task, "Reverse Engineer. Opens your own disc image, finds the game's code and maps how it works: the boot ELF, every function, the design doc. Drives the whole port and is the entry point of the Console pack. Reads ISO 9660 images without loading them whole, reads SYSTEM.CNF and the boot ELF (segments, CRC-32 and PCSX2 CRC, IRX modules), writes a starter PS2Recomp TOML with real keys only, and keeps console/STATE.md, the memory every /console-* skill reads first. Carries the PS2Recomp rules: never clean the build, never edit generated code or headers, a build gate, and a three-strike circuit breaker. Use when the user says ""port my PS2 game"", ""recompile my game"", ""open my ISO"", ""what's on this disc"", ""set up PS2Recomp"", ""where are we"", ""continue the port"", or at the start of any Console session."
  - jake-console-console-saves, Jake Console Console Saves, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-console-console-saves, .agents/skills/jake-console-console-saves, assess_for_task, "Save Manager. Brings your old memory card saves over, backs them up and syncs them to the cloud so you continue on any device. Reads PS2 memory card images (PCSX2 .ps2 and .mcd, raw 8 MB dumps, with or without ECC) and PCSX2 folder cards, lists every save with its title, copies saves into the port's folder memory card (mc0 next to the game's ELF), imports and exports single saves as .psu, makes timestamped zip backups, and syncs mc0 with an iCloud Drive, Dropbox, Google Drive or Syncthing folder. Card images are read only; mc0 is backed up before anything replaces a save; a sync never silently overwrites (when both sides changed it keeps both and reports a conflict). Use when the user says ""bring my saves over"", ""import my PCSX2 save"", ""my memory card"", ""back up my saves"", ""sync my saves"", ""continue on my Steam Deck"", ""restore a backup"", ""convert this .psu"", or before the first run of a port that needs a save."
  - jake-console-console-sound, Jake Console Console Sound, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-console-console-sound, .agents/skills/jake-console-console-sound, assess_for_task, "Sound Designer. Rips the music and sound effects and puts your own tracks back in. Decodes PS2 VAG files and raw SPU2 ADPCM from sound banks (.bd) to WAV, finds VAGs hidden inside archives and disc files, and encodes your own 16-bit WAV back to VAG at the original's sample rate, looping and size. Everything it writes goes under console/audio/; it refuses a replacement bigger than the original unless told otherwise, and never writes into the disc folder or the PS2Recomp checkout. Use when the user says ""rip the music"", ""extract the sound effects"", ""put my song in the game"", ""replace the soundtrack"", ""convert this VAG"", ""what is in this .bd"", ""the music loops wrong"", or after /console-levels finds audio files on the disc."
  - jake-console-console-tester, Jake Console Console Tester, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-console-console-tester, .agents/skills/jake-console-console-tester, assess_for_task, "Playtester. Runs the port again and again, reads every crash, ranks what to fix next and checks nothing broke. run.py starts ps2EntryRunner with your game's ELF under a hard timeout, kills the whole process tree, keeps the log in console/runs/ and calls the run PASS, HANG, CRASH or FAIL (soak repeats it N times; --input replays a controller script). triage.py reads the runtime's own log lines, clusters them by PC, names the function from your Ghidra CSV map, ranks them and names the /console-* skill that owns each; compare shows fixed, still there and new. abdiff.py finds the first divergence between PCSX2 and the port in register or memory dumps. Use when the user says ""run it"", ""does it boot"", ""test the port"", ""why did it crash"", ""what do I fix next"", ""did that break anything"", ""run it 100 times"", ""compare with PCSX2"", or after every build."
  - jake-day-trader-trader-alerts, Jake Day Trader Trader Alerts, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-day-trader-trader-alerts, .agents/skills/jake-day-trader-trader-alerts, assess_for_task, "Price Alerts. Rings when a price, a stop or the opening bell hits. Turns the trade plan into three alerts in one go (the stop, the target and ""flat by close"" at your flat-by time), plus above / below / stop / target levels, percent moves from the previous close, any time of day, and the NYSE opening bell, each ringing once so you are not spammed. Knows NYSE hours with the 2026 and 2027 holidays and 1:00 p.m. early closes, works out New York time itself, fetches free delayed quotes (Yahoo chart JSON, Stooq CSV) one ticker at a time, and writes trader/prices.json for sizing and the risk check. Use when the user says ""alert me when"", ""tell me if TSLA hits"", ""watch my stop"", ""watch my trade"", ""remind me to close by 3:55"", ""is the market open"", ""when does the market open"", ""get me a price"", or right after /trader-exit writes a plan."
  - jake-day-trader-trader-analyst, Jake Day Trader Trader Analyst, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-day-trader-trader-analyst, .agents/skills/jake-day-trader-trader-analyst, assess_for_task, "The Earnings Analyst. Reads a company's reported numbers straight from SEC EDGAR (XBRL company facts from its 10-Qs and 10-Ks, plus the latest earnings 8-K and its press release) and sums up what changed: revenue, gross, operating and net margins, net income and diluted EPS, quarter by quarter, each against the same quarter a year earlier, with the trailing twelve months. Reads an earnings call transcript when you paste one. Use when the user says ""how did Tesla's earnings look"", ""analyze the earnings"", ""what changed this quarter"", ""is revenue growing"", ""check the 10-Q"", ""compare margins"", ""sum up the call"", ""does it report this week"", or before trading a stock around its earnings."
  - jake-day-trader-trader-broker, Jake Day Trader Trader Broker, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-day-trader-trader-broker, .agents/skills/jake-day-trader-trader-broker, assess_for_task, "Order Executor. Sends approved orders to your broker, paper trading by default, never without your yes. Shows each order as a plain ticket (a bracket shows its stop-loss, take-profit and the max loss at the stop) plus the exact JSON for Alpaca's place_stock_order, records your yes word for word, then Claude's own Allow once / Deny card asks again. Builds the sell ticket that closes a day trade by your flat-by time, records fills, and logs each trade's max loss so trader-risk can hold the daily limit. Covers setting up Alpaca's official MCP server in Claude Desktop (paper by default, keys in env vars, never in chat), the Interactive Brokers connector, and setting order tools to ""Needs approval"". Use when the user says ""place the order"", ""buy it"", ""execute"", ""send it to my broker"", ""close my position"", ""flatten"", ""get me out"", ""connect Alpaca"", ""set up paper trading"", or after /trader-risk passes."
  - jake-day-trader-trader-budget, Jake Day Trader Trader Budget, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-day-trader-trader-budget, .agents/skills/jake-day-trader-trader-budget, assess_for_task, "Budget Manager. Sizes every position to your budget and your max loss per trade. Reads the trade plan from trader-exit (entry, stop, target), finds the whole shares that fit inside four limits (max loss per trade, position cap, max order, cash after your buffer), says which limit decided it, and writes ONE bracket order (entry, stop-loss, take-profit) to trader/orders.json in the exact shape of Alpaca's place_stock_order. A stop too far away for your max loss is a plain refusal, not a smaller order. Nothing is placed. Use when the user says ""how many shares"", ""size this trade"", ""how much should I buy"", ""I have $5,000"", ""I only want to risk $50 a trade"", ""set my rules"", ""keep 10% in cash"", or after /trader-exit writes a plan."
  - jake-day-trader-trader-entry, Jake Day Trader Trader Entry, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-day-trader-trader-entry, .agents/skills/jake-day-trader-trader-entry, assess_for_task, "Entry Timer. Watches a setup bar by bar and tells you the moment to get in. Reads free Yahoo 1-minute or 5-minute bars, builds the opening range (the first 15 minutes by default) and calls the entry on the first completed bar that CLOSES above the range high, or above a level you give it (like a 20-day high from the scanner), with an optional volume check. Says waiting and how far, triggered with the time and the price, expired, or not open yet, and writes trader/entry.json for /trader-exit. Long side only. It never places an order. Use when the user says ""tell me when to get in"", ""watch TSLA"", ""has it broken out"", ""did it break the opening range"", ""entry signal"", ""time my entry"", ""check my watchlist"", or after /trader-scanner and /trader-news, before /trader-exit."
  - jake-day-trader-trader-exit, Jake Day Trader Trader Exit, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-day-trader-trader-exit, .agents/skills/jake-day-trader-trader-exit, assess_for_task, "Exit Planner. Sets your stop and your target before you enter, so you know when to get out. Reads the entry from trader-entry (or a price you give), puts the stop at the opening-range midpoint by default (or the range low, your price, a percent, or a multiple of the ATR), rounds it down to the cent, and sets the target at 2R (or 1R, or your price). Refuses a stop at or above the entry, a target at or below it, or a stop too tight to survive the spread, and says why. Writes trader/plan.json for the Time Machine, the Budget Manager and Price Alerts. Long side only. Use when the user says ""where's my stop"", ""set my stop and target"", ""plan the exit"", ""when do I get out"", ""stop loss"", ""what's my R"", ""risk reward"", or right after /trader-entry triggers, before /trader-timemachine."
  - jake-day-trader-trader-news, Jake Day Trader Trader News, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-day-trader-trader-news, .agents/skills/jake-day-trader-trader-news, assess_for_task, "News Monitor. Tracks breaking news on every stock you watch and flags what moves it: Yahoo Finance headlines per ticker, each company's 8-K filings on SEC EDGAR (earnings, CEO changes, deals, restatements, bankruptcy) and how far each stock is from yesterday's close. Shows only what is new since the last check, newest first, in New York time, tags each item (earnings, analyst, deal, halt, regulatory, macro...) and never repeats one. Use when the user says ""any news on TSLA"", ""why is this moving"", ""what's the news on my watchlist"", ""morning briefing"", ""pre-market news"", ""monitor the news"", ""did anything break"", ""check the 8-Ks"", or after /trader-scanner finds setups."
  - jake-day-trader-trader-pelosi, Jake Day Trader Trader Pelosi, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-day-trader-trader-pelosi, .agents/skills/jake-day-trader-trader-pelosi, assess_for_task, "The Pelosi Tracker. Watches the stock trades members of Congress must disclose under the STOCK Act: reads the House Clerk's public Periodic Transaction Reports (PTRs) as soon as they are posted, alerts once per new filing, and turns each PDF into clean rows (who, owner, stock, ticker, buy or sell, options strike and expiry, trade date, amount range, how many days it took to disclose). Flags trades in stocks you hold. Senate reports are covered by a documented manual route. Use when the user says ""what is Pelosi buying"", ""track Nancy Pelosi"", ""Congress trades"", ""politician stock trades"", ""did any congressman buy X"", ""alert me when Pelosi files"", or ""run the Pelosi skill""."
  - jake-day-trader-trader-risk, Jake Day Trader Trader Risk, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-day-trader-trader-risk, .agents/skills/jake-day-trader-trader-risk, assess_for_task, "Risk Manager. Checks every trade against your limits and stops anything over them, before it can reach the broker. For a day trade: a stop is required, the loss at the stop must fit your max loss per trade (measured from the higher of the plan's entry and a fresh price), reward:risk must meet your minimum, the day's total risk must fit your daily loss limit, no more than your trades per day, and no new entries outside your entry window or when the market is closed. It also keeps the basics: blocked tickers, order size, position cap, cash buffer, margin, short sales, options and crypto, malformed or bad bracket orders, duplicates and a daily order limit. Getting out is never blocked by a day limit. Prints PASS or BLOCK with the reason and records the verdicts so trader-broker only shows an order that passed. Use when the user says ""check my order"", ""is this safe"", ""risk check"", ""does this break my rules"", ""can I take this trade"", ""how much have I risked today"", or before /trader-broker, always."
  - jake-day-trader-trader-scanner, Jake Day Trader Trader Scanner, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-day-trader-trader-scanner, .agents/skills/jake-day-trader-trader-scanner, assess_for_task, "Chart Scanner. Scans thousands of charts for setups: opening-range breakouts, flags, oversold bounces. Builds the list of US-listed common stocks, ordinary shares and ADRs from Nasdaq Trader's symbol directories, runs a pre-market scan of daily closes (20-day closing-high breakout, bull flag, reclaimed the 20-day average, oversold, oversold bounce) and an intraday opening-range breakout scan on 5-minute bars, then writes trader/watchlist.json for trader-news and trader-entry. Free Yahoo data, bar by bar. Use when the user says ""scan the market"", ""find me setups"", ""what is breaking out"", ""opening range breakouts"", ""scan for bull flags"", ""oversold stocks"", ""pre-market scan"", ""build my watchlist"", ""what should I look at today"", or at the start of a trading day before /trader-news."
  - jake-day-trader-trader-timemachine, Jake Day Trader Trader Timemachine, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-day-trader-trader-timemachine, .agents/skills/jake-day-trader-trader-timemachine, assess_for_task, "Time Machine. Replays every possible outcome of a trade before you risk a dollar: 10,000 simulated sessions plus every past time the setup fired. Takes the plan from trader-exit (entry, stop, target), rebuilds the rest of the day 10,000 times from the stock's own 5-minute bars over the last 60 days, and re-runs the same rule on every past session. Prints the odds of target first, stop first, or neither by the close, where the price sits at the close, the average R, the history, and one honest verdict, then hands off to /trader-budget. Use when the user says ""run the time machine"", ""replay this trade"", ""what are the odds"", ""simulate this trade"", ""monte carlo"", ""backtest this setup"", ""how often does this hit the target"", ""is this a coin flip"", or after /trader-exit writes a plan, before /trader-budget."
  - jake-duel-duel, Jake Duel Duel, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-duel-duel, .agents/skills/jake-duel-duel, assess_for_task, "Have an OpenAI model challenge Claude's answer, then defend or revise it through a short evidence-led debate. Use for ""duel this with ChatGPT"", ""face off this answer"", or an explicit request for a second model to critique an answer."
  - jake-founder-founder-board, Jake Founder Founder Board, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-founder-founder-board, .agents/skills/jake-founder-founder-board, assess_for_task, "Your board of directors. Puts a business idea in front of a three-member board, each a sub-agent reading the idea through one published framework: the Offers lens (from Alex Hormozi's $100M Offers), the Monopoly lens (from Peter Thiel's Zero to One) and the Product lens (from Walter Isaacson's biography of Steve Jobs). Each member scores the idea, names the risks that would kill it and votes fund, fund with conditions, or pass. Use when the user says ""test my business idea"", ""would this work"", ""pressure-test this"", ""what would a board say"", ""is this a good business"", or starts the founder pack on a new idea."
  - jake-founder-founder-brand, Jake Founder Founder Brand, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-founder-founder-brand, .agents/skills/jake-founder-founder-brand, assess_for_task, "Your brand designer. Names the business (with the trademark, domain and handle checks to run before falling in love with a name), writes the voice, a one-line promise and a tagline, and briefs the look: colours, type, logo and the first things a customer sees, so they match the positioning the marketing director chose. Use when the user says ""name my business"", ""brand this"", ""logo"", ""brand identity"", ""what should it look like"", ""tagline"", or ""brand voice""."
  - jake-founder-founder-cfo, Jake Founder Founder Cfo, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-founder-founder-cfo, .agents/skills/jake-founder-founder-cfo, assess_for_task, "Your CFO. Builds the unit economics of a business before money is spent: what one unit earns after its direct costs, the real profit margin at the planned volume, the break-even point in units a day, year 1 month by month, the cash needed before it pays for itself, how long the startup spend takes to earn back, and what happens if the price drops, sales come in low or costs rise. Every number traces to an input the user can check. Use when the user says ""find the profit margins"", ""do the numbers"", ""is this profitable"", ""break-even"", ""unit economics"", ""how much do I need to start"", or ""run the CFO""."
  - jake-founder-founder-competitors, Jake Founder Founder Competitors, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-founder-founder-competitors, .agents/skills/jake-founder-founder-competitors, assess_for_task, "Maps every competitor and the gap they leave. Finds the direct competitors, indirect ones and the substitutes a buyer would use instead, from public sources only, and records what each sells, at what price, how they position themselves and what their customers complain about in public reviews, every fact with a link. Ends with a positioning map and the gap the new business can own. Use when the user says ""who are my competitors"", ""is this market crowded"", ""what else is out there"", ""competitor analysis"", ""find the gap"", or ""who am I up against""."
  - jake-founder-founder-consumer, Jake Founder Founder Consumer, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-founder-founder-consumer, .agents/skills/jake-founder-founder-consumer, assess_for_task, "The consumer panel. Spins up a swarm of buyer sub-agents (default 100, --quick for 20) trained on the user's target customer, each with a different income, age, buying behaviour and objection, shows every one the same pitch, and runs the business through 100 buyer scenarios to see who buys, who doesn't, and why. Tallies the answers into buy rates by segment, the reasons people pass in their own words, what would flip a no, and price answers for founder-pricing. Use when the user says ""would people buy this"", ""test it on customers"", ""run the consumer panel"", ""simulate buyers"", ""who is my customer"", or ""validate demand""."
  - jake-founder-founder-launch, Jake Founder Founder Launch, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-founder-founder-launch, .agents/skills/jake-founder-founder-launch, assess_for_task, "Your launch lead. Builds a dated, step-by-step launch plan: a cheap real-world test first (a waitlist, a pre-sale or a pop-up with a real price, so real buyers confirm what the simulated panel said), then the countdown to opening day with owners and deadlines, the launch-day run sheet, and the first 30 days of what to measure and what to change. Use when the user says ""how do I launch"", ""launch plan"", ""when can I open"", ""launch checklist"", ""go live"", or ""soft open""."
  - jake-founder-founder-marketing, Jake Founder Founder Marketing, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-founder-founder-marketing, .agents/skills/jake-founder-founder-marketing, assess_for_task, "Your marketing director. Turns the buyer panel and the competitor map into positioning, the channels the target customer actually uses, a 30-day launch campaign with dated posts and ads, the first ten hooks, a budget split and the numbers to watch. Every message answers an objection real or simulated buyers raised. Use when the user says ""how do I market this"", ""marketing plan"", ""launch campaign"", ""how do I get customers"", ""where do I advertise"", ""write my ads"", or ""positioning""."
  - jake-founder-founder-offer, Jake Founder Founder Offer, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-founder-founder-offer, .agents/skills/jake-founder-founder-offer, assess_for_task, "Builds an offer too good to refuse. Lists every problem the buyer hits on the way to the result they want, turns each into a solution, trims to what is cheap to deliver and valuable to the buyer, and stacks it with honest bonuses, a guarantee the CFO can afford, real urgency and a clear name. Scores it on the value equation (outcome, likelihood, time, effort) and re-tests it on a quick buyer panel. Use when the user says ""make my offer better"", ""why won't people buy"", ""what should I include"", ""guarantee"", ""bonuses"", ""grand slam offer"", or after the panel shows people passing."
  - jake-founder-founder-ops, Jake Founder Founder Ops, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-founder-founder-ops, .agents/skills/jake-founder-founder-ops, assess_for_task, "Your operations manager. Works out how the business actually runs on day one: suppliers and what they cost, who works when, the step-by-step routines for opening, serving or shipping and closing, the tools to run it, the licences and permits to check, and a risk register with what to do when each thing goes wrong. Feeds real costs back to the CFO. Use when the user says ""how do I run this"", ""operations"", ""suppliers"", ""staffing"", ""SOPs"", ""what do I need to open"", ""permits"", or ""day one""."
  - jake-founder-founder-plan, Jake Founder Founder Plan, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-founder-founder-plan, .agents/skills/jake-founder-founder-plan, assess_for_task, "Your business planner. Compiles everything the other founder skills wrote (the board's verdict, the competitors, the buyer panel, pricing, the offer, the CFO's numbers, marketing, brand, operations and the launch plan) into one business plan with a verdict at the top that is computed from the numbers, never written by hand: Profitable, Not yet (with the failing numbers) or Incomplete. Adds an executive summary and a one-page version for a partner, lender or investor. Use when the user says ""write my business plan"", ""put it all together"", ""is it profitable"", ""give me the plan"", or at the end of the founder pack."
  - jake-founder-founder-pricing, Jake Founder Founder Pricing, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-founder-founder-pricing, .agents/skills/jake-founder-founder-pricing, assess_for_task, "Finds the price buyers will actually pay. Reads the consumer panel's four price answers per buyer into a Van Westendorp price-sensitivity range (too cheap, a bargain, getting expensive, too expensive), sets it against what competitors really charge and against the CFO's margin, and recommends a price, a price ladder (good / better / best) and an opening offer to test. Use when the user says ""how much should I charge"", ""price this"", ""is $X too expensive"", ""pricing strategy"", ""what price"", or after the consumer panel."
  - jake-hunter-hunter-apply, Jake Hunter Hunter Apply, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-hunter-hunter-apply, .agents/skills/jake-hunter-hunter-apply, assess_for_task, "The Application Assistant. Fills the user's job applications from their own saved answers and leaves every one as a draft for them to review and submit: maps each form question to hunter/profile.json (name, links, work authorization, sponsorship, start date, relocation and more), flags what only the user can answer (salary, voluntary self-identification, anything not in the profile), runs a per-application checklist (tailored resume, cover letter, research, warm intro), fills the form in the user's browser with Claude in Chrome and stops before Submit. Use when the user says ""apply to this job"", ""fill out the application"", ""fill the Greenhouse form"", ""prep my application"", ""what's left before I apply"", or ""save it as a draft""."
  - jake-hunter-hunter-connector, Jake Hunter Hunter Connector, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-hunter-hunter-connector, .agents/skills/jake-hunter-hunter-connector, assess_for_task, "The Connector. Finds the hiring manager for a role (from the posting, the team page and a LinkedIn search the user runs), researches them from public professional information only, works out their likely work email with a confidence, drafts a personalized email and a LinkedIn note, and keeps the conversation going with polite, rule-bound follow-ups until a coffee chat is booked on the user's calendar. Nothing goes out without the user's yes for that exact message, every message is sent from the user's own accounts, and the stop rules end a thread at the first no. Use when the user says ""find the hiring manager"", ""reach out to the team"", ""get me a warm intro"", ""email the manager"", ""set up a coffee chat"", ""who is hiring for this role"", or ""follow up with Maya""."
  - jake-hunter-hunter-cover, Jake Hunter Hunter Cover, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-hunter-hunter-cover, .agents/skills/jake-hunter-hunter-cover, assess_for_task, "Cover Letter Writer. Writes a specific cover letter for every application: addressed to the hiring manager or the team, opening with something real about the company or the team from the research brief, one paragraph of proof from the tailored resume (a result with a number), why this team, and a clear ask, in 150 to 400 words. Then checks it with cover.py: company, role and team named, at least one concrete proof point, no banned cliches, no leftover placeholders, no other company's name pasted in, every number traceable to the resume, reading level. Use when the user says ""write a cover letter"", ""cover letter for Google"", ""do I need a cover letter"", ""make this letter better"", ""check my cover letter"", or after /hunter-resume."
  - jake-hunter-hunter-followup, Jake Hunter Hunter Followup, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-hunter-hunter-followup, .agents/skills/jake-hunter-hunter-followup, assess_for_task, "Follow-up Manager. Sends polite follow-ups so no thread goes cold, and stops before anyone feels chased. Every morning it reads hunter/pipeline.json and lists what is due today: follow-ups on unanswered outreach, replies waiting on you, drafts waiting for your yes, applications with no news after 10 days, thank-you notes after interviews and coffee chats, and anyone the stop rules have closed (first ""no"", 2 follow-ups, 21 days of silence, a stop request honoured forever). Drafts each message from a polite template; you approve, it goes out from your account, and it is logged. Use when the user says ""follow up"", ""who do I need to follow up with"", ""nudge"", ""they haven't replied"", ""check on my application"", ""thank-you note"", or every morning."
  - jake-hunter-hunter-interview, Jake Hunter Hunter Interview, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-hunter-hunter-interview, .agents/skills/jake-hunter-hunter-interview, assess_for_task, "Interview Coach. Runs mock interviews with the questions this company actually asks, from a question bank that cites each company's own published interview-prep pages (Google, Meta, NVIDIA, Netflix, Amazon) and marks everything else as community-reported. Shows the company's interview loop, asks one question at a time, checks every answer for Situation, Task, Action, Result and a number, coaches the weak part, logs the session and tells you what to practice next. Use when the user says ""mock interview"", ""practice interview"", ""prep me for Google"", ""what does Amazon ask"", ""Leadership Principles"", ""behavioral questions"", ""STAR"", ""system design practice"", ""interview tomorrow"", or when a role moves to screen or interview."
  - jake-hunter-hunter-linkedin, Jake Hunter Hunter Linkedin, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-hunter-hunter-linkedin, .agents/skills/jake-hunter-hunter-linkedin, assess_for_task, "The LinkedIn Optimizer. Rewrites the user's LinkedIn headline, About, skills and experience for the job they want, using only what is true, then checks the draft against LinkedIn's field limits (headline, About, skills count, position title and description) and against the keywords of the target job description, with a before/after report: coverage, required terms, what was gained and what is still missing. The user pastes the final text into LinkedIn themselves. Use when the user says ""optimize my LinkedIn"", ""rewrite my headline"", ""fix my About section"", ""LinkedIn for this job"", ""what skills should I list"", or ""make recruiters find me""."
  - jake-hunter-hunter-research, Jake Hunter Hunter Research, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-hunter-hunter-research, .agents/skills/jake-hunter-hunter-research, assess_for_task, "The Company Researcher. Researches each company the user is applying to and writes a one-page brief in hunter/companies/: the business from its own SEC filings (latest 10-K, 10-Q, recent 8-Ks with what each one is about), news from the company's own blogs, the culture in the company's own words, the team the user would join, and the interview loop with a source on every line (official prep pages for Google, Meta, NVIDIA, Netflix and Amazon, everything else marked community-reported). Use when the user says ""research Google"", ""tell me about this company"", ""company brief"", ""prep me for Meta"", ""what's their interview process"", ""what does this team do"", or before a coffee chat or interview."
  - jake-hunter-hunter-resume, Jake Hunter Hunter Resume, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-hunter-hunter-resume, .agents/skills/jake-hunter-hunter-resume, assess_for_task, "Resume Writer. Rewrites your resume for each role so it reads like the job description, using only what is true: it mirrors the posting's own words for skills you really have, moves buried results into strong bullets (a number, a strong verb, one line), reorders for the role, and asks you about anything the posting wants that the resume does not show. Scores the match from 0 to 100 with a published formula (minimum qualifications, preferred qualifications, bullet strength, sections) and runs a truth check that fails if the rewrite adds a number or a skill that was not in your original. Use when the user says ""rewrite my resume"", ""tailor my resume"", ""ATS score"", ""beat the ATS"", ""match my resume to this job"", ""resume for Google"", ""improve my bullets"", or after /hunter-scout picks a role."
  - jake-hunter-hunter-salary, Jake Hunter Hunter Salary, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-hunter-hunter-salary, .agents/skills/jake-hunter-hunter-salary, assess_for_task, "Salary Negotiator. Benchmarks the role and scripts your counter-offer. Turns an offer into total compensation year by year (base, bonus target, equity with its real vesting schedule including back-loaded ones, sign-on), compares offers side by side, pulls wage percentiles from the U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics (OEWS) for your occupation and area, adds pay ranges printed in job postings with their URL, and writes a counter range and a polite script that cites every number. Never invents a market number. Use when the user says ""I got an offer"", ""negotiate my salary"", ""is this offer good"", ""compare offers"", ""counter offer"", ""what should I ask for"", ""total compensation"", ""RSU vesting"", or when a role reaches the offer stage."
  - jake-hunter-hunter-scout, Jake Hunter Hunter Scout, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-hunter-hunter-scout, .agents/skills/jake-hunter-hunter-scout, assess_for_task, "The Job Scout. Finds the best open roles for the user's profile and ranks them by fit: pulls live listings from public job boards that need no login (Greenhouse, Lever, Ashby, NVIDIA's Workday board, Netflix's careers search), filters by title, place, remote and how recent, scores every listing 0-100 against hunter/profile.json with the reasons (title, skills, location, seniority, pay range, freshness), writes hunter/jobs.json and adds the user's picks to the pipeline. Gives the manual route for Google, Meta and Amazon, whose careers sites cannot be read by a script. Use when the user says ""find me jobs"", ""best listings for me"", ""scout roles"", ""what's open at Google"", ""search Software Engineer jobs"", ""rank these jobs"", or ""where should I apply""."
  - jake-hunter-hunter-tracker, Jake Hunter Hunter Tracker, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-hunter-hunter-tracker, .agents/skills/jake-hunter-hunter-tracker, assess_for_task, "Pipeline Tracker. Tracks every role, contact and next step in one pipeline: hunter/pipeline.json, the single file every hunter skill reads and writes. Adds and updates roles and contacts, moves roles through the stages (saved, applied, screen, interview, onsite, offer, rejected, withdrawn), shows a summary by stage, what is coming up this week, what has gone stale, and exports CSV for a spreadsheet. Owns the pipeline schema and validates it after every change. Use when the user says ""show my pipeline"", ""where am I with each application"", ""add this job"", ""I applied"", ""I got an interview"", ""I got rejected"", ""what's next"", ""what's stale"", ""export my applications"", or ""track this""."
  - jake-illegal-codes-67, Jake Illegal Codes 67, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-illegal-codes-67, .agents/skills/jake-illegal-codes-67, assess_for_task, "Runs the task through six agents in parallel, each locked to a different strategy, then a seventh judge ranks the six attempts and synthesizes a final answer that steals the strongest part of each; invoke via /67 for high-stakes or open-ended work where a single attempt would leave quality on the table."
  - jake-illegal-codes-aura-farming, Jake Illegal Codes Aura Farming, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-illegal-codes-aura-farming, .agents/skills/jake-illegal-codes-aura-farming, assess_for_task, "Maximum-aesthetic mode for any visual deliverable (Meta ads, slide decks, landing pages, social graphics, posters, UI) that bans every AI-slop tell, forces a real design direction, and audits the result before shipping; invoke via /aura-farming whenever a visual is being created and it needs to look like a designer made it."
  - jake-illegal-codes-china-maxing, Jake Illegal Codes China Maxing, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-illegal-codes-china-maxing, .agents/skills/jake-illegal-codes-china-maxing, assess_for_task, "Session mode that translates every sub-agent prompt into Mandarin before dispatch (more meaning per character, fewer tokens) while keeping code, identifiers, and all user-facing output in English; invoke via /china-maxing at the start of any session that will fan out sub-agents and the token bill matters."
  - jake-illegal-codes-crash-out, Jake Illegal Codes Crash Out, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-illegal-codes-crash-out, .agents/skills/jake-illegal-codes-crash-out, assess_for_task, "Anti-hallucination mode where Claude drafts an answer and then becomes obsessed with proving itself wrong, attacking every claim with tools and counter-evidence and shipping only what survives; invoke via /crash-out on factual questions, debugging, research, or any answer where confident-and-wrong is expensive."
  - jake-illegal-codes-larp, Jake Illegal Codes Larp, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 1, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-illegal-codes-larp, .agents/skills/jake-illegal-codes-larp, assess_for_task, "Startup idea analyzer that channels a 24-year-old founder with Euro Summer photos and a $100M raise for a ChatGPT wrapper, runs the idea through a rigorous teardown underneath the bit, and assembles the strongest possible business model and pitch; invoke via /larp when the user shares a business, app, or product idea worth pressure-testing."
  - jake-instagram-ig-audit, Jake Instagram Ig Audit, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-instagram-ig-audit, .agents/skills/jake-instagram-ig-audit, assess_for_task, "Post-mortem on what the user has already posted - which reels actually worked, why, and what to stop making. Use when the user pastes their Instagram insights or past posts and asks ""what's working"", ""why did this flop"", ""read my analytics"", ""audit my content"", or wants to know what to do more of."
  - jake-instagram-ig-caption, Jake Instagram Ig Caption, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-instagram-ig-caption, .agents/skills/jake-instagram-ig-caption, assess_for_task, "Write the Instagram caption - the line that survives the ""... more"" cut, the body, the single ask, the search terms and the three hashtags - and lint it before it goes out. Use when the user says ""write the caption"", ""caption this"", ""what do I put in the description"", has a reel or a carousel ready and needs the text, or asks about hashtags."
  - jake-instagram-ig-carousel, Jake Instagram Ig Carousel, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill jake-instagram-ig-carousel, .agents/skills/jake-instagram-ig-carousel, assess_for_task, "Build an Instagram carousel - the cover that earns the swipe, slide-by-slide copy, and the 1080x1350 files to upload. Use when the user says ""carousel"", ""slides"", ""swipe post"", ""turn this into a carousel"", or has a list-shaped or step-shaped idea that would die as a single image."
