  - php-pro, Php Pro, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill php-pro, .agents/skills/php-pro, assess_for_task, "Write idiomatic PHP code with generators, iterators, SPL data structures, and modern OOP features. Use PROACTIVELY for high-performance PHP applications."
  - pick-ui-library, Pick Ui Library, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 1, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill pick-ui-library, .agents/skills/pick-ui-library, assess_for_task, "Pick the right library for a given frontend task from a curated, opinionated list , numbers, OTP inputs, charts, command menus, virtualization, drag and drop, toasts, state, styling, and more. Only runs when explicitly invoked; it does not trigger on its own."
  - pinterest-growth, Pinterest Growth, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill pinterest-growth, .agents/skills/pinterest-growth, assess_for_task, "The Pinterest growth playbook for 2026. Use when someone wants to ""grow on Pinterest,"" ""get traffic from Pinterest,"" ""a Pinterest strategy,"" a pin cadence/board structure, or to turn blog/product content into pins. Pinterest is a visual SEARCH engine where keyword-optimized, fresh, vertical pins compound into evergreen outbound traffic , optimise for discoverability + clicks, not in-the-moment engagement. Uses the PINS framework. Reads brand-profile + voice-builder first. The agent drafts pins + the schedule; WoopSocial schedules/publishes pins; metrics come from native Pinterest Analytics; nothing is fabricated. For ""Pinterest SEO"" / ""rank my pins"" / keyword titles-descriptions route to pinterest-seo; for designing the pin image route to pinterest-pin-design. Pairs with content-recycling."
  - pinterest-pin-design, Pinterest Pin Design, Domain & Research Extensions, Specialized, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill pinterest-pin-design, .agents/skills/pinterest-pin-design, assess_for_task, "The Pinterest pin design skill -- the visual half that pairs with pinterest-seo's keyword layer. Use when someone wants to design a pin, a Pinterest pin image, a pin text overlay, fresh pin variations for an existing URL, or board covers. Designs and briefs the 2:3 (1000x1500) vertical pin: one focal point, a keyword text overlay readable at feed size, brand-consistent template, safe zones, and 3-5 visually distinct FRESH designs per destination URL. Uses the SAVED framework. Reads brand-profile + the destination + the pinterest-seo keyword first. A HUMAN or an image/design tool (ideogram/canva/nano-banana/a designer) creates the final raster; WoopSocial publishes the finished pin image + title + description + board + link. No misleading pins, no repin-as-fresh dupes, engagement never fabricated. Distinct from pinterest-seo (the keyword layer -- they PAIR), pinterest-growth (the strategy), design-and-templates (the template system), and ideogram/canva (render the raster this briefs)."
  - pinterest-seo, Pinterest Seo, Technical SEO, SEO & Discovery, 2, AGY CLI|Gemini|Claude Code|Codex, bin/agyos skill pinterest-seo, .agents/skills/pinterest-seo, assess_for_task, "The Pinterest SEO / search-ranking skill -- the keyword layer that pairs with pinterest-pin-design's visual. Use when someone wants pins to rank in Pinterest search, needs keyword research, or wants keyword-optimized pin titles/descriptions/boards. Pinterest is a visual search engine where keywords and relevance rank you, not followers. Uses the FOUND framework. Reads brand-profile + the pin's destination first. The agent researches real queries (autocomplete + Guided Search + Trends; never fabricates volume), writes the keyword-led title + a natural description (no stuffing), specs the on-pin overlay keyword, and advises boards + link. WoopSocial publishes the pin's title + description + board + link; profile/bio, board setup, alt text, Rich Pins, and Trends/Analytics stay native/human. No stuffing; Pin->Board->Page must match; fresh pins, not dupes. Distinct from pinterest-pin-design (the visual), pinterest-growth (the strategy), and social-seo (cross-cutting search)."
